  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 952 PM MDT Mon May 11 2026\n\nUpper level high pressure has taken control of our weather for the\nnext couple of days. Thankfully this is not June or our high\ntemperatures would be well above 100 degrees. As it is high\ntemperatures on Wednesday will flirt with the triple digit mark at\na few lowland locations. Back to Tuesday, our highs in the\nafternoon will be around 10 degrees above average under clear \nskies. The upper level ridge will begin to push east on Wednesday \nas an upper level trough approaches from the west. As I mentioned,\nWednesday looks to be the hottest day of the week, with a slight \nchance (10 to 20%) that El Paso could see their first 100 degree \nhigh temperature of the year. As the upper level ridge pushes off\nto the east we will see a weak upper level trough trailing just \nbehind the ridge. The trough will have very little surface \nmoisture to work with, but we could see a few dry thunderstorms in\nthe Gila Wilderness.\n\nFor Thursday through Saturday, we will see a weak zonal or\nsouthwest flow across the region. This will keep us very warm with\nhigh temperatures running 5 to 8 degrees above average. No real\nstrong winds or rain chances through Saturday. On Sunday, an\napproaching upper level trough will give us some breezy afternoon\nwinds with high temperatures continuing to run several degrees\nabove average.",
